@prefix : <http://example.org/> .
# The template's SECOND triple puts `?t` — bound to a triple term — into the
# subject of a triple term NESTED in the object, which RDF 1.2 admits no more
# than it admits an asserted triple-term subject: a triple term nests only in
# the OBJECT of another triple term. §16.2 skips that instantiation instead of
# erroring, and emitting it instead would produce a document PurRDF's own
# readers refuse. The first triple is the control: it consumes the same row, so
# an empty result would mean the WHERE matched nothing rather than that the
# skip fired.
:r1 :reifies <<( :a :knows :b )>> .
